{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 136, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-to-output residual where none existed gives a larger gain than swapping out an existing conv or pool on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the residual skip on edge 0->3 hurts optimization much more than removing a conv or avg-pool there."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty 0->3 edge with a conv adds capacity, while replacing an existing skip with a conv destroys the beneficial residual path."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 0->2 already absent, cutting 0->1 disconnects nodes 1 and 2 from the input and collapses most of the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 0 is none, node 1 is dead, so adding a conv revives edges 2 and 4 as well and yields a larger gain than upgrading a skip or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 0->1 is none, node 1 carries only zeros, so a conv on 1->2 adds nothing."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 2->3 removed, node 2 never reaches the output, so improving its input edge has no effect."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a useful 3x3 conv costs more accuracy than deleting a weak avg-pool or a redundant skip."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Avg-pool edges are typically harmful in NAS-Bench-201, so removing one helps or barely hurts, while removing a conv or skip hurts."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Putting avg-pool on an empty edge is near-neutral, but swapping it in for a strong 3x3 conv on 2->3 clearly reduces accuracy."}], "tok": 30375, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "none"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3",